---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';

const effectiveDate = '9 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of service — GoServe"
  description="The terms governing use of GoServe's web app, mobile app, and API for cafes and restaurants in Nepal."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms of service" lede={`Effective date: ${effectiveDate}`} />

  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <p>
        These terms govern use of GoServe&rsquo;s web app, mobile app, and API (together, the
        &ldquo;Service&rdquo;), operated for cafes and restaurants in Nepal. By signing in and using the
        Service, you and/or your employer (&ldquo;you&rdquo;, &ldquo;Workspace&rdquo;) agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        GoServe is a business-to-business tool. Individual staff accounts are created and managed by a
        Workspace owner/admin &mdash; there is no public self-registration inside the app. You must be
        authorized by your Workspace to use the Service under that Workspace.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You&rsquo;re responsible for keeping your login credentials (email OTP access, or the Google account
        you sign in with) secure, and for activity that happens under your account. Tell us promptly if you
        suspect unauthorized access.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>use the Service for any purpose other than operating your Workspace&rsquo;s cafe/restaurant business;</li>
        <li>attempt to access data belonging to a Workspace you are not a member of;</li>
        <li>interfere with the Service&rsquo;s operation or attempt to circumvent its security;</li>
        <li>use the Service in a way that violates applicable law, including Nepal&rsquo;s tax (VAT) and consumer protection requirements.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Workspace data and ownership</h2>
      <p>
        Data entered into a Workspace (orders, menu, inventory, staff records, reports) belongs to that
        Workspace. Workspace owners/admins control who on their team can access it. We act as the processor
        of that data on the Workspace&rsquo;s behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>
        eSewa and Khalti payments are processed directly by those providers via their QR-based flow; GoServe
        is not a party to those payment transactions and does not hold your card or wallet credentials.
        Subscription/billing terms for the GoServe product itself are set out separately in your
        Workspace&rsquo;s plan agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and support</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep the Service available and responsive, including an offline mode that queues actions
        when connectivity drops and syncs once it&rsquo;s restored, but we don&rsquo;t guarantee uninterrupted
        availability. Contact <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> for support.
      </p>

      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p>
        A Workspace owner may close their Workspace, or remove a staff member&rsquo;s access, at any time. We
        may suspend or terminate access for a violation of these terms or applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimers and liability</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided &ldquo;as is.&rdquo; To the maximum extent permitted by law, GoServe is not
        liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from use of the Service. Nothing
        here limits liability that cannot be limited under Nepali law.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We&rsquo;ll update the effective date above when these terms change, and will give notice of material
        changes.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Nepal.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-section {
    padding-block: clamp(16px, 3vw, 40px) clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px);
  }
</style>
